# ===========================================
# RSYNC EXCLUDES FOR: make push (Local → HA)
# MORE RESTRICTIVE - Protect HA's runtime state!
# ===========================================

# Database and log files
home-assistant_v2.db*
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log*

# Custom add-ons and themes (managed separately)
custom_components/
custom_icons/
themes/

# Runtime/cache directories
.cloud/
deps/
tts/
.uuid
__pycache__/

# Large directories not needed for config management
backups/
image/
tmp_backups/
www/

# Secrets (real passwords live on HA, local file is placeholder)
secrets.yaml

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp

# ===========================================
# CRITICAL: on-HA tooling — NEVER delete
# /homeassistant/claude-code-ha/ holds ha-api / ha-ws and survives HA OS
# updates. It does not exist locally, so without this exclude `rsync --delete`
# wipes the tooling this whole workflow depends on.
# ===========================================
claude-code-ha/

# ===========================================
# Add-on runtime state — managed by the add-ons, not by us.
# Local copies are stale; pushing them rolls back live state.
# zigbee2mqtt: database.db / state.json / coordinator_backup.json ARE the
# Zigbee network (device pairings). Overwriting them can break the mesh.
# ===========================================
zigbee2mqtt/
esphome/

# Node-RED flows have a dedicated path: `make pull-nr` / `make push-nr`,
# which also restarts the a0d7b954_nodered add-on. A plain push would
# overwrite flows without restarting, so the add-on would ignore them.
node-red/

# HA brand/icon cache — regenerated at runtime
.cache/

# ===========================================
# On-HA files that do not exist in this repo.
# NOTE: /config is a SYMLINK to /homeassistant, so these are the same dir.
# .env holds the HA-side API token used by ha-api / ha-ws — deleting it
# breaks the tooling. CLAUDE.md is installed on HA by claude-code-ha.
# ===========================================
.env
.env.*
CLAUDE.md
*.bak-*

# ===========================================
# HA runtime files — must never be overwritten with stale local copies.
# A stale .HA_VERSION can trigger a spurious version migration on start.
# ===========================================
.HA_VERSION
.ha_run.lock

# ===========================================
# CRITICAL: NEVER PUSH .storage/ TO HA
# These contain runtime state that HA manages:
# - Integration configs (Shelly, Tuya, etc.)
# - Entity/device registries (renames, disables)
# - Dashboards created via UI
# - Authentication and sessions
# All changes should be made via HA UI or API
# ===========================================
.storage/
